                        "entry_id": "dc049d20-5bdd-3efe-90c0-590569a28d04",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To make gathers in textiles by drawing together parallel threads."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fa0652aa-f84e-3d35-93b9-993ccf262245",
                        "entry_id": "dc049d20-5bdd-3efe-90c0-590569a28d04",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To bake (a raw egg removed from its shell) in a baking dish."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "86524501-1e6b-4fc6-b175-9fb3270b7444",
                                "sense_id": "fa0652aa-f84e-3d35-93b9-993ccf262245",
                                "text": "The Creole eggs arrived in a ramekin, shirred on a bed of Virginia ham julienne and topped with a robust, spicy tomato sauce of Creole derivation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "920af04d-af21-4439-aad5-c34b88a5ec3b",
                                "sense_id": "fa0652aa-f84e-3d35-93b9-993ccf262245",
                                "text": "But her favorite way to express their simplicity is to shirr them. It's an old-fashioned technique that essentially means baking an egg. In her version, the eggs in ramekins are simmered in seasoned cream that reduces slightly into a soft sauce."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
